the introduction to bioinformatics  course is an introduction to the field  of bioinformatics or the intersection of  informatics and biology it speaks about  the opportunities that come with the  available big data and methods for its  analysis for research in industry  including healthcare agriculture  environmental sciences Public Health and  more biology is rapidly acquiring the  character of a data science billions of  data points on genes proteins and other  molecules are compiled in large files  and systematically studied analyzing  this data will lead to more knowledge  and understanding about living organisms  including human health  biotechnology crops and livestock this  course will give an overview of  bioinformatics for students biologists  and clinicians the influx of data  associated methodologies and data driven  research makes bioinformatics for Life  Sciences as prominent as the emergence  of computers for the tech industry the  course is divided into three sections  introduction to Big Data bioinformatics  bioinformatics and healthcare  transitional bioinformatics and all of  them can be completed in under two hours  of study the course will provide  important information terminology and  perspectives from experts in this  exciting field there are three sections  that can be completed in about 2 hours  of study with a quiz at the end  the course can be taken by anyone  without any special knowledge in related  fields after signing up and completing  your profile you'll be able to see your  progress and notice points you've earned  accumulate based on this activity you  can acquire certificates of completion  for this course as well as others on the  edu T bio info platform as an  introductory course you will also learn  about our project-based approach at  learning bioinformatics we take datasets  from high impact publications and  convert them into online learning  experiences each subsequent course you  take will have a practical application  that demonstrates how bioinformatics can  be used these projects will fall under  certain specializations such as oncology  neuroscience agro tech and others the  specializations provide domain  experience and explain basic  bioinformatics concepts related to that  subject as a result anyone starting on  this journey in bioinformatics can start  developing a project of their own by  seeing how experts analyze their data  and achieve research results you can  start developing a research question of  your own identify the appropriate type  of data you should be using and then  plan your analysis this introductory  course leads into multiple courses and  projects that can serve as a springboard  into the world of bioinformatics in  subsequent courses we will be using the  T bio info platform to process big  datasets this platform is built from  multi-omics integration and analysis of  structured data with advanced methods  such as machine learning and  mathematical modeling after you've set  up your account make sure to try out our  analytical platform you can do so by  filling out the form at server T bio  info this analytical platform will  provide hands-on experience for anyone  to apply the learn skills to interesting  datasets with color coded logical maps  explanation of methods detailed input  and output formats as well as  reproducible workflows this course  provides a broad overview but is  structured to offer significant depth  even for the experienced after  completing the short introduction you'll  be inspired to continue learning about  this exciting field of bioinformatics  this program has been tested in multiple  universities around the world and  reviewed by experts in the field of  bioinformatics we are excited that you  joined so let's start learning
 

